body.description:
Let's create a new analysis task. In data/raw/S2 you have the temporal serie of both atmospheric correction. Find date that are available for both and compute the difference in reflectance for each pixel of the image.&#x20;
The output should be a map showing the median of delta R for B2, B3, B4, and B8 in one row, and another row showing the standard deviation of the deltaR for those same bands. The final figure should be a patchwork of 8 maps (4 med + 4 sd). Minimise the text at the maximum, nothing about technical details, and choose color palett that are meaningfull and maximise visualisation of differences between pixel.&#x20;

Another graph will show the temporal series of deltaR, x is time and y is deltaR. each point is plotted and a gam is used to visualise the curve. This plot should be a facet of 2 plot one on top of the other, median and sd of deltaR. Everything is accompagned with a scientific, ready for publication methods section and results.
